  "issuedISO": "2026-11-01T15:46:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "Surf along north facing shores will continue to see High Surf Advisory level conditions through Monday with the swell peaking tonight before slowly dropping Monday. Offshore NDBC buoy 51101 continues to show long period energy in the 14 to 16 second bands. Another advisory level northwest swell is possible Thursday into Friday, and moderate to large surf action appears to continue into the weekend. The current moderate, medium period south swell will remain elevated this evening before declining on Monday. South shore surf will be tiny through much of the week with little southerly background energy reaching the islands. East- facing shores will see an increase in trade wind swell as strong northeast winds fill in Monday. Surf along east- facing shores will stay choppy as trades sustain through much of the week.",
